e) Further, as there were five claimants, deduction of 1/4th has been rightly made towards personal expenses;
f) As per postmortem report, age of deceased was taken to be 42 years, and therefore, multiplier of 14 has been correctly applied;
g) On this basis, learned Tribunal has correctly calculated loss of dependency as Rs.45,000/- x 14 =
Rs.6,30,000/-;
h) Rs.25,000/- has been granted towards funeral expenses;
i) Rs.5,000/- has been granted towards loss of estate;
j) Rs.1,00,000/- has been granted towards consortium;
k) Hence, total compensation awarded comes to Rs.7,60,000/-.
